  {
   "id": "pMjWRF1RCgAJ",
   "from": "Juergen Niedballa",
   "author": "0b86ca0cb4b615b0",
   "date": "2017-11-20T05:50:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: 'date.test. in detection histories",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div>the main problem is your argument <span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">day1 = &quot;setup&quot;</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\">. </font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\">You have 3 options for argument </font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">day1</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\">. it can be &quot;station&quot;, &quot;survey&quot;, or a date, formatted like this: &quot;2016-12-31&quot;. &quot;setup&quot; is not possible. I will add a proper error message for this case. The object date.test is used in internal tests of the function and should not be visible.</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\">Besides this, </font><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"> </span><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">occasionStartTime </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">needs to be defined differently. </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">occasionStartTime = 00:00 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">will work, but only by chance. In R, the colon : is a shorthand for a sequence of numbers. Thus 00:00 means: sequence from 0 to 0 (which is 0) and will thus work. If you set it to e.g. 06:00 it will be a sequence from 6 to 0 (equivalent to </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">c(6,5,4,3,2,1,0) </font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">and </font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">seq(6,0)</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">) and will not work in this function), The correct way to use the argment </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">occasionStartTime </font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">is to give a single number. If you want midnight, it is </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">occasionStartTime = 0 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">and if you want 12 noon, it is </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">occasionStartTime = 12</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">.</span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
